<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Terror (Hungary)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Red Terror in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was the campaign of repression carried out by the Hungarian Soviet Republic in 1919 against its real and supposed enemies. Revolutionary tribunals and armed squads, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibor-szamuely">Tibor Szamuely</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenin-boys">Lenin Boys</a>, executed several hundred people, many after peasant revolts. It was followed after the regime's fall by a larger White Terror.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-terror-hungary.jpg" alt="Red Terror (Hungary)" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tormay, Cécile (1876–1937). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_terror_victim,_Hungary_-_Spring_1919.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
